WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:02.940
<b>SHINOYAMA</b>

00:04.250 --> 00:07.990
This is quite a mansion, even by the 
imperial aristocracy's standards.

00:08.440 --> 00:10.110
Oh, my.

00:10.110 --> 00:12.710
Welcome home, Uncle Polka.

00:12.710 --> 00:16.240
Aw, and I bet on him making a run for it.

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
<b>Shizuki Shinoyama (11)</b>

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
<b>Polka's Nephew</b>

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
<b>Polka's Niece</b>

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
<b>Kazuki Shinoyama (11)</b>

00:12.880 --> 00:16.240
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

00:17.020 --> 00:18.030
Yes.

00:18.390 --> 00:19.990
I did make a promise.

00:20.330 --> 00:22.020
Good grief.

00:22.020 --> 00:25.850
You honestly came waltzing back here?

00:25.020 --> 00:28.840
<b>Polka's Nephew
President of Shinoyama Security</b>

00:25.020 --> 00:28.840
<b>Takeru Shinoyama (26)</b>

00:25.020 --> 00:28.840
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

00:26.400 --> 00:29.320
What happened to your 
"journey of self-discovery"?

00:26.730 --> 00:28.840
<b>I'm going on a journey
of self-discovery.</b>

00:29.650 --> 00:32.810
I found a new me in Shinjuku.

00:33.160 --> 00:33.760
Oh?

00:34.170 --> 00:35.100
Now,

00:35.560 --> 00:38.840
would you explain the young 
lady accompanying you?

00:38.840 --> 00:39.720
Well...

00:40.050 --> 00:42.230
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:42.230 --> 00:44.390
I am Misaki Sakimiya.

00:44.800 --> 00:46.790
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

02:24.960 --> 02:28.930
Really? You were about to jump to your 
death when Polka talked you down?

02:28.930 --> 02:29.970
Yes.

02:29.970 --> 02:33.900
If not for Polka-kun, I wouldn't be here.

02:34.480 --> 02:38.080
And he's saved me several more times since.

02:38.760 --> 02:39.680
Hmm...

02:40.000 --> 02:43.800
It appears Polka really did "find a new him."

02:44.540 --> 02:45.310
Although...

02:45.980 --> 02:50.130
I never expected he'd wind up with the 
daughter of Sakimiya Steel's owner.

02:50.130 --> 02:53.940
My family's business no longer exists.

02:54.870 --> 02:56.000
Pardon me.

02:56.590 --> 02:59.130
Your parents helped me a 
lot when I was younger.

02:59.990 --> 03:03.720
What happened to them was... 
truly unfortunate.

03:05.210 --> 03:07.080
The current head of the 
Shinoyama family is Rozan.

03:07.080 --> 03:13.880
<b>Rozan Shinoyama                  Kanon Shinoyama</b>

03:07.080 --> 03:13.880
<b>Gaku Shinoyama                                Polka Shinoyama</b>

03:07.080 --> 03:13.880
<b>Kiri Shinoyama        Takeru Shinoyama          Suzuka Shinoyama              Sayo Shinoyama             Kazuki Shinoyama         Shizuki Shinoyama</b>

03:07.450 --> 03:11.090
His eldest son, Gaku Shinoyama, is 48.

03:11.090 --> 03:13.880
Polka is the son of Rozan's second wife.

03:14.110 --> 03:17.150
So the brothers were born 
more than 30 years apart.

03:17.970 --> 03:21.210
Then there's your nephew, Takeru Shinoyama.

03:20.050 --> 03:25.680
<b>Takeru Shinoyama</b>

03:21.590 --> 03:25.310
As far as Polka's relatives go, 
he's definitely the one to watch out for.

03:26.010 --> 03:28.430
He's the president of 
Shinoyama Security, and—

03:29.640 --> 03:39.650
Shinoyama Security? 
A lot of former police big-shots 
end up there. 
They hush up scandals by eliminating 
inconvenient people. 
Rumor has it they control all 
the less savory parts 
of the Shinoyama Group.

03:38.030 --> 03:39.650
You sure know a lot.

03:40.250 --> 03:45.320
Well, Takeru's dangerous because he runs 
that shady operation at just 26 years old.

03:46.560 --> 03:48.520
That must have been hard on you.

03:48.520 --> 03:52.050
Listen, if you're ever in trouble, 
you can count on us for help.

03:52.050 --> 03:52.870
Kiri.

03:52.870 --> 03:55.770
Don't make careless promises 
about people's livelihoods.

03:55.770 --> 03:58.970
Oh, don't be like that, Takeru-san.

03:59.360 --> 04:02.050
<b>Takeru's Wife</b>

03:59.360 --> 04:02.050
<b>Kiri Shinoyama (24)</b>

03:59.360 --> 04:02.050
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

03:59.360 --> 04:02.050
She'll be like part of the family.
Won't that be lovely?

04:02.280 --> 04:05.800
I'm saying you should 
consider her feelings first.

04:06.570 --> 04:10.270
In any case, you're welcome 
as a friend of the family.

04:10.610 --> 04:12.580
Make yourself at home.

04:12.580 --> 04:14.990
Thank you so much for your kindness.

04:14.990 --> 04:17.560
<i>Amazing. She plays her part perfectly.</i>

04:17.950 --> 04:20.220
<i>I'd better make sure I don't 
give myself away either.</i>

04:20.650 --> 04:23.720
<i>I spent last night cramming about manners,
 but I'm still nervous.</i>

04:24.820 --> 04:26.750
What's with that shark doll?

04:27.160 --> 04:29.100
Is it me, or does it move sometimes?

04:29.100 --> 04:30.400
Well, this is—

04:30.400 --> 04:32.060
The Sharkborg from Hell.

04:32.060 --> 04:33.160
Sayo-nee?

04:33.160 --> 04:37.080
That design is from the climax of Part Two.

04:34.770 --> 04:37.080
<b>Polka's Niece     Unemployed</b>

04:34.770 --> 04:37.080
<b>Sayo Shinoyama (20)</b>

04:34.770 --> 04:37.080
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

04:37.390 --> 04:42.020
The first three were absolute classics, 
but then they made the sharkborg humanoid.

04:42.020 --> 04:45.050
Ditching all the shark elements made me sick.

04:45.050 --> 04:49.150
Personally, I didn't mind the 
hot-girl orcadroid in five.

04:49.150 --> 04:52.560
But then, at the end, 
the sharkborg's mouth shoots...

04:50.750 --> 04:56.050
Oh, Master Polka! I'm so glad you're safe!

04:56.050 --> 04:56.730
Huh?

04:56.730 --> 04:57.940
Oh, thanks.

04:57.940 --> 04:58.860
<i>Who's he?</i>

05:00.020 --> 05:03.090
<i>Huh? A relative? What's his name?</i>

05:04.650 --> 05:08.490
You might be even more of a 
go-getter than your father!

05:05.590 --> 05:08.490
<b>Some Relative</b>

05:05.590 --> 05:08.490
<b>(Rozan Shinoyama's Niece's Husband) 52</b>

05:05.590 --> 05:08.490
m 0 0 l 330 0 330 65 0 65

05:09.620 --> 05:11.770
Um... Where is everyone else?

05:11.770 --> 05:13.950
At work, of course.

05:13.950 --> 05:16.810
Our parents are overseas.

05:16.810 --> 05:21.140
That leaves Takeru-oniisama, 
who happened to have a day off,

05:21.140 --> 05:24.650
Kiri-oneesama, and Sayo-oneesama, 
who's unemployed.

05:24.650 --> 05:26.580
Just call me a bedroom security officer.

05:27.530 --> 05:29.470
I couldn't handle guarding the whole house.

05:29.470 --> 05:32.100
Apart from us, no one else is here today.

05:32.100 --> 05:35.540
Hey, now, Kazuki.

05:35.920 --> 05:39.020
Don't forget the master of the house.

05:39.460 --> 05:42.570
<b>Head of the Shinoyama Group</b>

05:39.460 --> 05:42.570
<b>Rozan Shinoyama (79)</b>

05:39.460 --> 05:42.570
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 65 0 65

05:39.690 --> 05:42.190
Do you want to make your grandpa cry?

05:42.840 --> 05:45.850
Grandfather! Is it safe for you
 to be up and about?

05:45.850 --> 05:48.620
Yeah, this is one of my good days.

05:49.160 --> 05:50.660
Oh, right. Sayo.

05:50.660 --> 05:51.450
Yeah?

05:51.450 --> 05:57.410
I watched that movie you recommended, 
<i>Lost Vacation</i>. I liked it.

05:57.650 --> 05:59.880
Really? Great.

06:00.210 --> 06:03.910
Next, try <i>47 Meters Under 
the Sea</i> or <i>Panic Market</i>.

06:04.380 --> 06:06.260
<i>All shark movies, I'm guessing.</i>

06:06.260 --> 06:08.010
Why, hello, sir!

06:08.010 --> 06:10.720
I'm so glad to see you 
on the way to recovery!

06:10.720 --> 06:11.960
This is perfect timing.

06:11.960 --> 06:15.200
I wanted to discuss the 
pharmaceutical division with you.

06:15.200 --> 06:19.610
I'm semi-retired. Talk to Gaku
 about business issues.

06:19.610 --> 06:22.760
I... I realize that, but—

06:22.760 --> 06:23.690
Hey.

06:24.890 --> 06:26.570
Are you gonna make me repeat myself?

06:28.170 --> 06:30.850
P-Pardon me, sir!

06:31.920 --> 06:33.270
Grandfather.

06:34.220 --> 06:36.390
Don't give me that look.

06:36.390 --> 06:40.750
If he'd made it sound urgent, 
I would've heard him out.

06:41.170 --> 06:42.040
Now,

06:42.450 --> 06:43.240
Polka.

06:43.240 --> 06:45.250
Y-Yes?!

06:45.640 --> 06:48.470
Don't you have something to say to me?

06:54.910 --> 06:59.060
I'm, um, sorry for running away from home?

07:00.980 --> 07:02.760
No, idiot.

07:04.500 --> 07:07.050
You start with "I'm home."

07:09.400 --> 07:10.830
I'm... home?

07:10.830 --> 07:14.410
I overheard that young lady's story,

07:14.640 --> 07:17.620
but I'd like to hear what you have to say.

07:18.040 --> 07:20.600
Come with me to the tatami room in the annex.

07:20.600 --> 07:21.960
O-Okay.

07:22.510 --> 07:27.630
Sorry, miss. Entertain yourself 
in the garden for a bit.

07:27.630 --> 07:28.550
I'd love to.

07:31.680 --> 07:35.730
That's it? I hoped Polka 
was gonna get chewed out.

07:35.730 --> 07:37.880
Maybe he's about to be.

07:38.350 --> 07:40.760
Close... Close...

07:40.760 --> 07:44.170
The fire is close.

07:45.530 --> 07:47.360
You, a fortune teller?!

07:48.000 --> 07:50.020
Well, what do you know!

07:50.020 --> 07:54.570
And a distant relative of the young lady's 
runs an exclusive club in Shinjuku?

07:54.570 --> 07:59.160
Yes. And she rented us a room 
in an unused building.

07:59.160 --> 08:01.590
That took guts.

08:01.590 --> 08:04.130
Anything else worth mentioning?

08:04.130 --> 08:07.740
Well, a policeman caught 
one of my friend's drones.

08:07.740 --> 08:09.050
Come again?!

08:09.050 --> 08:12.230
<i>Thank goodness. I think I can fool him.</i>

08:12.230 --> 08:15.550
Oh, I almost forgot. Tell me one last thing.

08:15.550 --> 08:17.550
What is it, Dad?

08:18.090 --> 08:20.770
Who are you?

08:23.410 --> 08:25.590
What do you mean, Dad?

08:26.240 --> 08:27.380
What I said.

08:27.380 --> 08:32.040
Still, it's strange. You certainly 
look and sound like Polka.

08:32.040 --> 08:32.950
That's because—

08:32.950 --> 08:36.780
But you're not. You aren't Polka.

08:37.040 --> 08:39.810
I don't understand, Dad.

08:39.810 --> 08:41.250
You're not making sense.

08:42.830 --> 08:44.080
Listen.

08:44.680 --> 08:47.170
Don't take me for a fool.

08:47.470 --> 08:53.130
I may have one foot in the grave,
but I've survived my share of crises.

08:53.770 --> 08:58.170
And, most importantly, I'm his father. 
Sense doesn't enter into it.

08:59.070 --> 09:00.350
<i>I see.</i>

09:00.610 --> 09:02.810
<i>So this is what a parent is.</i>

09:03.230 --> 09:05.130
C'mon, he's my darling son.

09:05.130 --> 09:07.030
Gimme something to sweeten the deal.

09:07.560 --> 09:11.530
<i>He's nothing like the ones I've known.</i>

09:11.870 --> 09:16.490
Actually, I've got one more question for you.

09:16.850 --> 09:20.460
Where's the real Polka? Is he alive?

09:21.170 --> 09:22.290
Well...

09:25.140 --> 09:26.620
Whoa, there.

09:26.620 --> 09:29.500
Kazuki and Shizuki may be in danger.

09:29.500 --> 09:30.380
What?

09:30.380 --> 09:33.960
I promised to protect those children,

09:34.270 --> 09:35.590
so I'm leaving.

09:35.590 --> 09:38.120
Please trust me. I'll explain later.

09:40.410 --> 09:43.040
I've got no clue what you're talking about...

09:43.040 --> 09:44.310
But go on.

09:44.310 --> 09:45.640
Thank you.

09:49.060 --> 09:51.630
No normal person moves like that.

09:52.730 --> 09:56.450
You should've just killed him, Your Lordship!

09:56.450 --> 10:01.120
I'm not heartless enough to slay someone 
with my son's face just like that.

10:03.950 --> 10:06.790
Well, damn. That sounds serious.

10:12.900 --> 10:14.780
Suzuka-oneechan.

10:14.780 --> 10:18.180
Listen, we went exploring in the
 woods out back, and...

10:18.180 --> 10:21.970
My purse is gone. I think I dropped it.

10:21.970 --> 10:26.050
Don't worry. I'll find it for you.

10:26.050 --> 10:26.980
You will?

10:26.980 --> 10:28.140
Thanks!

10:33.120 --> 10:34.740
There it is!

10:34.740 --> 10:37.450
Hey, I gave her this purse.

10:37.450 --> 10:39.370
I guess she really liked it.

10:39.370 --> 10:41.820
I see you managed to infiltrate.

10:42.830 --> 10:43.750
Who's there?

10:44.630 --> 10:47.030
What happened to that face's original owner?

10:47.030 --> 10:48.600
I burned him up.

10:48.600 --> 10:51.030
Thoroughly, until even his bones were ash.

10:51.030 --> 10:53.220
I... I see.

10:53.950 --> 10:57.240
Now, I'd say preparations 
will take... about two years.

10:57.240 --> 10:58.790
That's a long time to wait.

10:58.790 --> 11:04.280
It would be easier to just burn a few 
people and make it look like an accident.

11:04.280 --> 11:08.860
For example, say those twins 
were playing with fire.

11:10.090 --> 11:11.690
What's wrong?

11:12.560 --> 11:13.690
Oh, nothing.

11:14.320 --> 11:18.030
But something smells lovely.

11:18.030 --> 11:22.740
Like soft flesh... 
that I'm just dying to burn.

11:24.810 --> 11:26.210
I need to warn them!

11:26.210 --> 11:28.840
Grandfather and Takeru-oniisama!

11:28.840 --> 11:30.850
Kazuki and Shizuki!

11:32.110 --> 11:32.750
What?

11:32.750 --> 11:33.540
It's hot...

11:37.880 --> 11:39.760
An explosion in the boiler room?!

11:39.760 --> 11:42.090
Hey! Where's Suzuka-sama?!

11:42.620 --> 11:44.580
Oh, thank goodness.

11:44.970 --> 11:47.270
You're both all right.

11:47.980 --> 11:49.300
Hurry. You need to run!

11:50.740 --> 11:51.710
What's wrong?

11:52.540 --> 11:54.970
Can't you hear me?

11:56.050 --> 11:58.780
Someone, anyone...

11:58.780 --> 12:00.030
Save these children!

12:02.740 --> 12:03.450
SOMEONE

12:02.780 --> 12:04.280
Someone...

12:03.450 --> 12:04.280
SOMEONE

12:04.280 --> 12:05.990
...save...

12:06.550 --> 12:08.490
...these children.

12:09.210 --> 12:09.950
Huh?

12:09.950 --> 12:10.730
What?

12:10.730 --> 12:11.710
Are you hurt?!

12:12.020 --> 12:15.050
Kazuki-sama! Shizuki-sama! There's a fire!

12:15.050 --> 12:16.040
A fire?!

12:16.040 --> 12:17.370
Follow me! You need to evacuate!

12:22.970 --> 12:24.480
No...

12:25.020 --> 12:26.510
No!

12:28.470 --> 12:30.680
Tokyo Detention House

12:29.560 --> 12:30.680
Iwa-san.

12:30.970 --> 12:35.410
Why are you going to consult 
a troublemaker like <i>him</i>?

12:35.410 --> 12:40.070
To crack this case, we'll need 
to go a little bit crazy.

12:40.360 --> 12:42.240
Only a little?

12:42.690 --> 12:43.950
I know, I know.

12:47.150 --> 12:53.050
But you can't deny that he's the 
closest to that thing we saw.

12:55.190 --> 12:56.750
Ten'a Sorimura.

12:57.290 --> 12:58.250
Or should I say...

12:58.490 --> 13:00.120
the Phantom Solitaire?

13:00.470 --> 13:04.720
You gave me that name. 
It's just a pun on my real one.

13:05.680 --> 13:09.180
But lately, it's been growing on me.

13:09.180 --> 13:10.900
Glad to hear it.

13:11.640 --> 13:12.930
Shakuzawa Building Fire Witness:
 "Flames are shooting from the broken windows"

13:11.640 --> 13:12.930
m 0 0 l 395 0 395 30 0 30

13:15.520 --> 13:17.590
I see. Fascinating.

13:17.590 --> 13:21.940
I don't know if it's coincidence or fate, 
but we've pinned that fire

13:21.940 --> 13:24.860
on a troublemaker. 
The Fire-Breathing Bug.

13:25.720 --> 13:29.070
They always leave the same message:

13:29.470 --> 13:34.330
"This world is a buggy program," 
meaning everything's all screwed up.

13:34.790 --> 13:37.720
We found it written at the scene.

13:37.720 --> 13:43.150
And just like in all their other crimes, 
the fire spread impossibly fast.

13:44.270 --> 13:46.590
So, I came up with a theory.

13:46.810 --> 13:48.760
They infiltrate their targets in disguise

13:49.050 --> 13:52.330
and take their time painstakingly 
preparing the ground.

13:52.330 --> 13:57.190
Just like bugs chewing through your 
house while you're none the wiser.

13:58.850 --> 14:01.610
Then they breathe fire out of the blue.

14:01.610 --> 14:03.490
This way! Hurry!

14:03.490 --> 14:05.440
There's an escape tunnel that leads outside!

14:05.440 --> 14:06.330
Okay!

14:07.950 --> 14:10.950
What's wrong, Kazuki?! Hurry up!

14:10.950 --> 14:11.870
Wait.

14:11.870 --> 14:15.250
There's no way out down here.

14:15.250 --> 14:20.040
Oh, no, little miss. I assure you there is.

14:20.040 --> 14:20.710
What?

14:20.940 --> 14:23.840
I've spent two years building it.

14:44.870 --> 14:46.570
Right in the nick of time!

14:46.950 --> 14:48.070
Um...

14:48.290 --> 14:52.410
I can't see you, but you can relax now, okay?

14:52.410 --> 14:55.870
Me and Polka-kun are gonna save these kids!

14:57.660 --> 14:58.790
Wow.

14:58.790 --> 15:00.870
You sure can take a beating.

15:01.640 --> 15:05.020
Well, I made my skin nice and thick.

15:05.020 --> 15:08.700
I only planned to snack on the twins today,

15:08.700 --> 15:11.380
but this is an unexpected feast.

15:11.380 --> 15:16.220
Polka-kun was right on the money! 
Good thing I was watching you!

15:16.490 --> 15:18.790
Now, get going. Run back upstairs.

15:18.790 --> 15:20.440
B-But...

15:20.840 --> 15:21.850
Go on!

15:25.000 --> 15:25.960
Let's go!

15:26.650 --> 15:30.070
I'm guessing you're one of us, mister.

15:30.390 --> 15:32.570
So you must've heard of me.

15:33.790 --> 15:36.030
Zaki the Killer Killer.

15:36.250 --> 15:40.000
I got a glimpse of you when I 
was scoping out Clarissa's bar.

15:40.930 --> 15:42.180
I knew it!

15:42.180 --> 15:46.670
You seemed scared of me when things 
got tense at Polka-kun's place.

15:47.430 --> 15:50.050
So that's what tipped you off.

15:50.050 --> 15:52.290
But that doesn't explain

15:52.290 --> 15:55.760
what you're doing with Polka Shinoyama!

15:57.600 --> 15:59.810
Did Rozan hire you?!

15:59.810 --> 16:02.120
Hmm... Not quite.

16:02.120 --> 16:03.980
But I'm not telling!

16:03.980 --> 16:05.060
Idiot!

16:12.270 --> 16:14.110
Are you even human?

16:15.680 --> 16:17.180
Y'know,

16:17.180 --> 16:21.910
I was sure you'd try to 
chase after those kids!

16:30.010 --> 16:32.260
You want to know why I didn't?

16:32.750 --> 16:34.090
That's simple.

16:34.090 --> 16:36.580
Because there's nowhere to run!

16:37.330 --> 16:38.600
Not for you,

16:38.870 --> 16:41.600
and not for those brats!

16:43.130 --> 16:44.580
Stay low to the ground.

16:45.130 --> 16:47.740
Maybe... we had this coming.

16:48.450 --> 16:52.010
I wonder... if Suzuka-oneechan's mad at us.

16:53.050 --> 16:56.110
She'd... She'd never...

16:58.320 --> 17:00.790
No, maybe she is.

17:01.760 --> 17:03.870
I mean, it was our fault.

17:04.400 --> 17:06.960
Of course she's mad.

17:10.240 --> 17:11.960
If we see her,

17:11.960 --> 17:14.850
let's say sorry together, Shizuki.

17:14.850 --> 17:15.930
Yeah.

17:23.820 --> 17:26.520
Suzuka-oneechan?

17:27.010 --> 17:28.060
Thank goodness.

17:29.980 --> 17:31.680
This time, I wasn't too late.

17:31.680 --> 17:33.430
Polka...?

17:34.280 --> 17:36.350
Remember what the fortune teller told you?

17:36.810 --> 17:38.970
You have a future.

17:39.600 --> 17:42.160
And she's not upset with you.

17:42.160 --> 17:43.080
What?

17:44.370 --> 17:48.470
Suzuka-san has never 
stopped caring for you.

17:50.180 --> 17:51.500
Where are the fire trucks?!

17:51.500 --> 17:52.890
They'll be here soon!

17:54.210 --> 17:56.340
Kazuki-sama! Shizuki-sama!

17:56.850 --> 17:58.200
I'm so glad you're safe!

17:59.200 --> 18:00.010
Now,

18:00.780 --> 18:04.010
shall we begin cleaning up after

18:04.680 --> 18:06.100
this misuse of fire?

18:07.790 --> 18:11.480
The Fire-Breathing Bug should 
have finished his job by now.

18:20.370 --> 18:25.330
That stubborn old bastard Rozan 
embarrassed me in front of everyone.

18:26.290 --> 18:29.260
I hope he gets a good whiff 
of his descendants roasting

18:29.260 --> 18:31.750
while he cries himself to death.

18:34.430 --> 18:35.420
It can't be!

18:35.750 --> 18:38.660
I had it all rigged perfectly!

18:38.660 --> 18:40.890
Fine. I'll withdraw for now 
and roast you all to—

18:40.890 --> 18:42.380
Where do you think you're going?

18:43.450 --> 18:47.520
Oh, Master Polka! You're safe!

18:47.520 --> 18:48.940
Don't bother pretending.

18:49.240 --> 18:51.990
Your soul's hue hasn't changed.

18:51.990 --> 18:56.110
And while I was too distracted 
by the twins to notice yesterday,

18:56.990 --> 18:59.490
it seems you've earned a lot of resentment.

18:59.770 --> 19:01.690
Give it back!

19:01.690 --> 19:03.700
My face! My face!

19:04.240 --> 19:05.250
What the—?!

19:05.660 --> 19:07.740
You went back to your male voice.

19:15.140 --> 19:19.230
That was a close one! I thought I was 
gonna die from oxygen deficiency!

19:20.560 --> 19:23.620
I'm impressed you saw 
through my disguise twice.

19:23.620 --> 19:25.200
Enough banter.

19:25.560 --> 19:29.520
If I could spare the mana, I would 
make your death last a century.

19:29.520 --> 19:33.070
Oh, I'm quaking in my boots. Don't get cocky.

19:33.070 --> 19:37.160
You sound like a delusional kid who 
thinks he just got superpowers.

19:37.160 --> 19:39.080
That reminds me

19:39.080 --> 19:42.990
of when I first learned how to do <i>this</i>!

19:46.810 --> 19:48.540
You're scared of fire?

19:48.540 --> 19:51.410
Then I'm not scared of you!

19:51.410 --> 19:53.420
Whoever you are,

19:53.420 --> 19:56.330
the flames will get you in the end!

19:56.330 --> 19:57.910
This ain't goodbye!

19:57.910 --> 19:59.630
Bugs are stubborn bastards!

19:59.630 --> 20:02.570
No matter how many you 
crush, we just keep coming!

20:03.560 --> 20:05.720
<i>Can I break through with my remaining mana?</i>

20:07.580 --> 20:10.700
<i>There are </i>two<i> living 
things beyond this fire?!</i>

20:11.040 --> 20:12.060
<i>And this hue is...</i>

20:18.830 --> 20:19.840
Lemmings.

20:19.840 --> 20:23.000
Wow, really? What do you 
think he's doing here?

20:29.120 --> 20:31.770
You think he wants us to keep this a secret?

20:31.770 --> 20:34.610
What's going on here?

20:37.690 --> 20:38.340
Ta...

20:38.340 --> 20:39.870
Takeru-kun.

20:39.870 --> 20:44.590
The police are escorting your 
arsonist friend to jail as we speak.

20:44.590 --> 20:45.600
Impossible!

20:45.600 --> 20:46.790
Er, I mean...

20:46.790 --> 20:48.620
I don't know what you're talking about!

20:50.930 --> 20:53.140
The D-Dragon Palace Agency?

20:53.440 --> 20:57.690
I don't recall giving them 
such a grandiose name.

20:58.090 --> 21:02.650
I simply brought all the people who do the 
Shinoyama Group's dirty work together.

21:03.530 --> 21:04.690
W-Wait!

21:04.690 --> 21:08.020
I was just being threatened 
by the Fire-Breathing Bug!

21:08.020 --> 21:11.010
I see. I suppose it all makes sense, then.

21:12.250 --> 21:17.330
Someone as stupid as you <i>would</i> think 
he could stand against my family.

21:21.060 --> 21:25.040
You've been lying to me 
this whole time, haven't you?

21:25.350 --> 21:26.970
You noticed?

21:26.970 --> 21:31.680
A master of disguise who spends 
ages preparing the scene?

21:31.900 --> 21:33.140
I don't think so.

21:33.140 --> 21:34.440
No!

21:34.440 --> 21:36.310
Not a chance!

21:36.310 --> 21:39.190
That's just some ordinary person gone wrong.

21:39.190 --> 21:41.150
A common criminal.

21:42.270 --> 21:45.510
He's not what you people 
would call a "troublemaker"—

21:45.510 --> 21:50.830
people who have surpassed human 
limitations without resorting to magic.

21:50.830 --> 21:56.320
Then again, some of what we do 
might as well be magic, I suppose.

21:56.320 --> 22:01.500
And while the Fire-Breathing 
Bug always leaves that message,

22:01.500 --> 22:05.640
it has a second part, known 
only to the police, doesn't it?

22:05.640 --> 22:11.540
But all the crime scenes you described 
were missing that second part.

22:11.540 --> 22:13.100
Am I wrong?

22:16.570 --> 22:19.250
Seriously, how did you find out about that?

22:21.810 --> 22:22.920
<i>Damn it!</i>

22:22.920 --> 22:25.820
<i>I'll find my opening, then roast 
these cops and their car, too.</i>

22:31.450 --> 22:33.230
N-No way...

22:33.230 --> 22:35.870
"This world is a buggy program..."

22:36.120 --> 22:37.830
I-It can't be.

22:37.830 --> 22:40.670
"...so it cries for the flame."

22:41.290 --> 22:44.550
The <i>real</i> Fire-Breathing Bug?!

22:45.550 --> 22:47.970
Se-Settle d-down-own-own.

22:47.970 --> 22:52.650
Fake bug wannabe wannabe 
bug-abe wannabe bug bug bug.

22:52.650 --> 22:54.720
Fake bugs...

22:54.720 --> 22:57.350
...must be... exterminated.

22:58.980 --> 23:00.400
I-It's hot! It's hot!

23:01.450 --> 23:02.690
Wh-What the—?!

23:03.260 --> 23:04.360
Get out!

23:07.720 --> 23:11.050
What the hell just happened?!

23:09.600 --> 23:14.990
<i>Goodness, that boy is wet as can be...</i>

23:15.340 --> 23:20.630
<i>He's weeping under a willow tree.</i>

23:21.000 --> 23:26.840
<i>Pitter-patter. Plop-plop. 
Splash, splash, splash.</i>

23:23.670 --> 23:24.650
<b>Fire Safety</b>

23:24.650 --> 23:30.570
<b>Fire Safety</b>
